  "description": "ADR 0366 Phase 4 \u2014 the full feature-composition catalog. THREE tiers: (1) `core` = the always-included substrate a distribution can never exclude (auth/orgs/chat/workflow-engine/billing/design-system + the always-on/graduated features); (2) `bundles` = sellable feature GROUPINGS (one per toggle `category`) an include-mode manifest selects by name; (3) STANDALONE = every registered feature that is neither core nor bundled \u2014 DERIVED (not listed here), individually selectable in an include-mode manifest's `features[]`. Phase-4 include semantics (a correction to P2's 'core = unbundled by construction'): the excludable universe is `registered \u2212 core`, so a standalone feature defaults OUT and is opted IN \u2014 the licensing-safe direction. INVARIANTS (gen-distribution --check enforces all): every core/bundle id is registered; no id is in two places; `core` is dependsOn-CLOSED (no core feature hard-depends on a non-core one \u2014 so every bundle/standalone the shop offers is actually buildable); an always-on feature (no toggleDefault) MUST be core. A new feature is auto-standalone-selectable unless added to core or a bundle.",
